-- schema_version: NOT bumped. Data-only (no DDL). Stays at 35 (row 35 = 0045).
--
-- ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING: this migration MUST be applied AFTER mig-0049.
--            Applying either alone leaves `export_lynceus.py` halting, which is
--            the DB-and-exports/-disagree state of MAC-275 I.1.
--
-- Purpose:   Correct a proven INGEST-SIDE TYPE-WRITE DEFECT. This is a
--            type-integrity correction, NOT a promotion. No row gains feed
--            visibility, no confidence changes, no device_category changes.
--            Rows entering `ble_uuid` do NOT thereby acquire GATT-binding
--            evidence; the MAC-477 rule is untouched and every row stays in the
--            §11 #13 unknown-category bin. Adjudicating what these devices ARE
--            remains MAC-568's lane.
--
--            ONE EXCEPTION, CEO-APPROVED AND REQUIRED: ARM 0 changes the
--            `description` content of THREE already-shipping feed entries by
--            carrying vendor attribution forward off rows this migration
--            supersedes. That is a feed change and it was decided at the feed
--            level — CEO_RATIFICATION.md §2, "approved, and required". The
--            emitted ENTRY SET is unchanged; only content moves.
--
-- CORRECTION TO THE FOLD JUSTIFICATION (CEO AMENDMENT A1, requirement 3).
--            An earlier draft of this file and PROOF.md §4 justified the fold on
--            each survivor having "strictly better typing and an
--            already-adjudicated device_category". That sentence is ACCURATE on
--            `identifier_type` and on `device_category`, and it is FALSE on
--            `manufacturer`, `confidence` and `source_type`. The prose is
--            preserved verbatim in PROOF.md §4 with the correction appended
--            rather than edited in place (Apply-time-correction discipline);
--            this header states the corrected claim directly:
--
--              The survivor is better TYPED and already CATEGORIZED. It is not
--              uniformly better. On 4 of 51 pairs the superseded SIG
--              primary_registry row is the ONLY carrier of vendor attribution
--              and the survivor is a crowdsourced row with manufacturer NULL;
--              ARM 0 exists precisely because the fold would otherwise destroy
--              that attribution. On the 11 EXACT-duplicate pairs the survivor is
--              WORSE on confidence (NULL vs 75) — see the A2 record below.
--
-- CONSEQUENCE RECORDED, DELIBERATELY NOT FIXED HERE (CEO AMENDMENT A2).
--            The 11 EXACT-duplicate survivors (42986-42996: Axon, Verkada,
--            Rhombus, Motive, Samsara) all carry `confidence = NULL`.
--            `export_lynceus.py:981-982` bins a NULL confidence as
--            `below_confidence_threshold` — it fails ANY floor — and 0 of the 11
--            appear in either committed export. The rows this migration folds
--            into them carry `confidence = 75`, which clears both floors.
--            So this fold converts those 11 adjudicated surveillance-vendor
--            rows from "one MAC-568 recategorization away from the feed" to
--            "unreachable until the NULL is fixed".
--            The fold is still correct: `superseded_by` is a soft delete, the
--            row stays queryable, and the alternative mints the MAC-570
--            duplicate-emitted-key defect this stack exists to remove. Setting
--            confidence on those 11 would PROMOTE high-value surveillance
--            vendors into the feed, which is a feed decision needing its own
--            evidence and its own gate, and it does not belong bolted onto a
--            type-integrity correction. Tracked at MAC-663.
--
-- The defect: Wave-J WideNet ingested `assigned_numbers/uuids/member_uuids.yaml`
--            (the SIG *Member UUID* registry) and wrote `identifier_type=
--            'ble_company_id'` (the SIG *Company Identifier* registry) on all
--            705 active rows. Each row's own provenance records the intended
--            type verbatim:
--              notes.source_row_key = 'J-1|ble_uuid|0xfeff|'
--            The type field of that key reads `ble_uuid` on 705 of 705 rows,
--            zero exceptions. The canonical row contradicts its own manifest.
--
-- Cohort basis — proven by SET-EQUALITY, not by the numeric threshold alone:
--            source_url = member_uuids.yaml  ->  705 rows
--            value >= 0xFC00                 ->  705 rows
--            src \ num = {}   num \ src = {}   SET-EQUAL: True
--            The two independent bases select the identical set, so the cohort
--            is not an artefact of either one.
--
-- Blast radius is bounded: across all 1,705 active `j_widenet` rows the ONLY
--            (source_row_key type != identifier_type) combination is
--            ('ble_uuid','ble_company_id') x 705. No other Wave-J type-write
--            defect exists.
--
-- ============================================================================
-- PARTITION — and why a flat 705-row retype is WRONG
-- ============================================================================
-- `ble_uuid` and `ble_service_uuid` BOTH map to the Lynceus wire type
-- `ble_uuid` (`db/validation/export_lynceus.py:108,118` — CP21 §4.4
-- alias-collapse). Expanding all 705 to the canonical 128-bit form and typing
-- them `ble_uuid` therefore collides with rows that ALREADY EXIST:
--
--   11 rows -> EXACT (identifier, identifier_type) duplicates of active
--              `ble_uuid` rows: Axon body_cam, Verkada + Rhombus cctv_camera,
--              Motive + Samsara automotive_telematics. There is NO UNIQUE index
--              on (identifier, identifier_type) — only the non-unique
--              `idx_identifiers_ident_type` — so SQLite would accept every one
--              of these SILENTLY.
--   40 rows -> same wire pattern as an active `ble_service_uuid`/`ble_service`
--              row under a DIFFERENT identifier_type, hence a different
--              argus_record_id (SAR-10 hashes `identifier_type|identifier`).
--              That is precisely the MAC-570 duplicate-emitted-key defect class
--              that mig-0049 exists to REMOVE — freshly minted in the same stack.
--
-- The feed-delta test is VACUOUS against this hazard: all 705 rows are
-- device_category='unknown', so none of them emit today and ADDED/REMOVED both
-- read 0 whether or not the 51 collisions are created. The hazard is latent and
-- fires the moment MAC-568 recategorizes — and MAC-568's screen holds 18 of
-- these rows, including id 38372, which is MAC-611's own B3 guard fixture and
-- which collides EXACTLY with id 42986 (Motive, ble_uuid, automotive_telematics).
--
-- So the 705 are partitioned:
--   654  RETYPE  ble_company_id -> ble_uuid, value expanded to the canonical
--                128-bit form (lowercase, matching the 11 existing 128-bit
--                `ble_uuid` rows byte-for-byte).
--    51  FOLD    superseded_by = <surviving row id>, CP32 §9 <other_id>
--                SUCCESSOR semantics — NOT a self-loop. Every one of the 51 has
--                a surviving active twin carrying the same normalized value
--                from the same registry with strictly better typing and an
--                already-adjudicated device_category, so a
--                withdrawal-without-successor self-loop would be the wrong
--                tri-state and would lose the fold target. Same treatment
--                mig-0049 applies to its own 20 MAC-570 duplicates.
--
-- Folding a duplicate is NOT adjudication: the survivor already exists, is
-- already active, and is already categorized. Nothing is decided about what the
-- superseded row's device is.
--
-- The 9 active `ble_company_id` rows below 0xFC00 are GENUINE company
-- identifiers (sources: tagfinder.py, an APK, and company_identifiers.yaml) and
-- are NOT touched by this migration.
-- ============================================================================

-- ASSERTION MECHANISM: `CREATE TEMP TABLE t(ok INTEGER CHECK (ok=1))` +
-- `INSERT ... SELECT CASE`. NOT `SELECT CASE WHEN ... THEN RAISE(ABORT,...)`:
-- SQLite rejects RAISE() outside a trigger-program with a PARSE ERROR, which
-- `sqlite3 db < file` reports on stderr while CONTINUING to execute the rest of
-- the script. An unenforced guard that prints an error and lets the UPDATEs
-- commit anyway is worse than no guard. This idiom is mig-0049's (line 186).

-- `.bail on` IS LOAD-BEARING, NOT COSMETIC. `sqlite3 db < file` does not stop
-- on error by default, and a CHECK-constraint failure aborts only the offending
-- INSERT -- not the transaction. Without this line a FAILED PRECONDITION prints
-- to stderr and then the UPDATEs run and COMMIT anyway, which is strictly worse
-- than having no precondition at all. Verified empirically on a sandbox copy:
-- without `.bail on` this migration applied in full on top of a failing PRE-1.
-- NOTE FOR MAC-611: mig-0049 has the same exposure -- same assertion idiom, no
-- `.bail on`. Flagged to the CEO on MAC-642, not silently patched here.
.bail on

PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;
BEGIN IMMEDIATE;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- PRE-CONDITIONS
-- Fail closed. Every count is re-derived from the DB, none are hard-coded
-- forecasts carried over from a dispatch.
CREATE TEMP TABLE _scope AS
  SELECT id FROM identifiers
  WHERE superseded_by IS NULL AND identifier_type='ble_company_id'
    AND source_url='https://bitbucket.org/bluetooth-SIG/public/raw/main/assigned_numbers/uuids/member_uuids.yaml';

CREATE TEMP TABLE _pre AS SELECT
  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM identifiers WHERE superseded_by IS NULL) AS active,
  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM identifiers WHERE superseded_by IS NULL AND identifier_type='ble_company_id') AS bci,
  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM identifiers WHERE superseded_by IS NULL AND identifier_type='ble_uuid') AS bu,
  -- Whole-table, NOT active-only. Superseding does not touch `manufacturer`,
  -- and neither does the retype arm, so the ONLY thing that can move this
  -- number is ARM 0. A whole-table count makes POST-12 immune to the 51 rows
  -- leaving the active set, which an active-only count would confound.
  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM identifiers WHERE manufacturer IS NULL) AS mfr_null;

-- PRE-1 is an ORDER GATE, not an absolute row-count pin.
--
-- An absolute pre-state count is exactly the defect that stalled mig-0049: it
-- pinned 43124, MAC-537's ingest landed, and the CHECK then failed against
-- 43160. This migration applies AFTER mig-0049, so any absolute count written
-- here at authoring time is stale before it is ever run (43160 pre-0049 ->
-- 43140 post-0049). The invariant that actually matters is ORDERING, so assert
-- ORDERING directly: mig-0049 must already have folded its 20 MAC-570 rows.
-- Applying 0051 first leaves the export halting on gate 2 (MAC-275 I.1).
-- MAC-642 PRE-1 FAIL: mig-0049 has not been applied — order is load-bearing, apply 0049 first
CREATE TEMP TABLE _mac642_pre_1fail (ok INTEGER CHECK (ok = 1));
-- NOT pinned to an exact count. mig-0049 is still IN FLIGHT and owned by
-- MAC-611: it currently marks 18 rows (13 UPDATE statements deactivating 20
-- rows; the two Flock `ssid_exact` rows 22908/22909 carry no marker). Pinning
-- 0051 to that bookkeeping would couple this migration to a number it has no
-- business asserting and would rot the moment MAC-611 revises its own file --
-- which is the exact lesson mig-0049's own header draws at line 157. Existence
-- is what ordering requires; the substantive property is POST-5.
INSERT INTO _mac642_pre_1fail(ok) SELECT CASE WHEN ((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM identifiers
                  WHERE json_valid(notes)
                    AND json_extract(notes,'$.mac611_supersession.audit_issue')='MAC-611') < 1) THEN 0 ELSE 1 END;
-- MAC-642 PRE-2 FAIL: active ble_company_id is not 714
CREATE TEMP TABLE _mac642_pre_2fail (ok INTEGER CHECK (ok = 1));
INSERT INTO _mac642_pre_2fail(ok) SELECT CASE WHEN ((SELECT bci FROM _pre) <> 714) THEN 0 ELSE 1 END;
-- MAC-642 PRE-3 FAIL: active ble_uuid is not 13
CREATE TEMP TABLE _mac642_pre_3fail (ok INTEGER CHECK (ok = 1));
INSERT INTO _mac642_pre_3fail(ok) SELECT CASE WHEN ((SELECT bu FROM _pre) <> 13) THEN 0 ELSE 1 END;

-- PRE-4: json_valid sweep over the ENTIRE mutation scope before any json_set.
-- A json_set against a CP39-style text-suffixed notes blob RAISES (MAC-611);
-- this proves the scope is clean rather than assuming it.
-- MAC-642 PRE-4 FAIL: non-JSON notes inside the mutation scope
CREATE TEMP TABLE _mac642_pre_4fail (ok INTEGER CHECK (ok = 1));
INSERT INTO _mac642_pre_4fail(ok) SELECT CASE WHEN ((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM identifiers
                  WHERE identifier_type='ble_company_id' AND superseded_by IS NULL
                    AND (notes IS NULL OR json_valid(notes)=0)) <> 0) THEN 0 ELSE 1 END;

-- PRE-5: the cohort's two independent bases must still be set-equal.
-- MAC-642 PRE-5 FAIL: member_uuids.yaml cohort is not 705
CREATE TEMP TABLE _mac642_pre_5fail (ok INTEGER CHECK (ok = 1));
INSERT INTO _mac642_pre_5fail(ok) SELECT CASE WHEN ((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM identifiers
                  WHERE superseded_by IS NULL AND identifier_type='ble_company_id'
                    AND source_url='https://bitbucket.org/bluetooth-SIG/public/raw/main/assigned_numbers/uuids/member_uuids.yaml') <> 705) THEN 0 ELSE 1 END;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- PRE-6 .. PRE-8 — added by CEO AMENDMENT A1 (CEO_RATIFICATION.md §2).
-- ARM 0 below mutates FOUR rows that are NOT `ble_company_id` and therefore sit
-- OUTSIDE PRE-4's sweep. PRE-4 is scoped `identifier_type='ble_company_id'`; the
-- four ARM 0 targets are `ble_service_uuid`. Relying on PRE-4 to cover them
-- would be a scope error of exactly the kind MAC-598 records — reading the
-- selector's prose instead of its literal branch condition. They get their own
-- guards.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- PRE-6: json_valid over the ARM 0 mutation scope. ARM 0 calls json_set on these
-- four rows; a CP39-style text-suffixed notes blob would RAISE.
-- MAC-642 PRE-6 FAIL: non-JSON notes inside the ARM 0 attribution-carry scope
CREATE TEMP TABLE _mac642_pre_6fail (ok INTEGER CHECK (ok = 1));
INSERT INTO _mac642_pre_6fail(ok) SELECT CASE WHEN ((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM identifiers
                  WHERE id IN (22864,22865,22876,22878)
                    AND (notes IS NULL OR json_valid(notes)=0)) <> 0) THEN 0 ELSE 1 END;

-- PRE-7: all four survivors are still UNATTRIBUTED. This fails CLOSED if any
-- other lane backfills one of them first: ARM 0 must never silently overwrite a
-- manufacturer someone else adjudicated. Re-derived, not assumed.
-- MAC-642 PRE-7 FAIL: an ARM 0 target already carries a manufacturer
CREATE TEMP TABLE _mac642_pre_7fail (ok INTEGER CHECK (ok = 1));
INSERT INTO _mac642_pre_7fail(ok) SELECT CASE WHEN ((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM identifiers
                  WHERE id IN (22864,22865,22876,22878)
                    AND manufacturer IS NULL AND superseded_by IS NULL) <> 4) THEN 0 ELSE 1 END;

-- PRE-8: the four DONOR rows still carry the exact vendor strings being carried
-- forward, byte-for-byte. Without this, ARM 0 would write a hard-coded literal
-- that the donor no longer says — an attestation, not a carry-forward.
-- MAC-642 PRE-8 FAIL: a donor row's manufacturer is not the value ARM 0 carries
CREATE TEMP TABLE _mac642_pre_8fail (ok INTEGER CHECK (ok = 1));
INSERT INTO _mac642_pre_8fail(ok) SELECT CASE WHEN ((SELECT COUNT(*) FROM identifiers
                  WHERE superseded_by IS NULL AND identifier_type='ble_company_id'
                    AND ((id=37817 AND manufacturer='Google LLC')
                      OR (id=38025 AND manufacturer='Qingping Technology (Beijing) Co., Ltd.')
                      OR (id=38137 AND manufacturer='Samsung Electronics Co., Ltd.')
                      OR (id=38159 AND manufacturer='Apple Inc.'))) <> 4) THEN 0 ELSE 1 END;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- THE GO GATE — `.bail on` ALONE IS NOT ENOUGH, AND THIS IS WHY.
--
-- `.bail on` is a sqlite3 CLI *dot-command*. It is honoured by `sqlite3 db <
-- file`, and it is a NO-OP under every other application path: Python's
-- `sqlite3.Connection.executescript()`, `apsw`, an ORM migration runner, or a
-- copy-paste of this file's SQL into a session. Under any of those, a failed
-- precondition aborts only its own INSERT and every UPDATE below then runs and
-- COMMITS — the exact half-applied outcome MAC-641/MAC-642 recorded (15
-- assertions enforcing nothing while 705 UPDATEs committed).
--
-- So the guard is made STRUCTURAL rather than procedural: `_mac642_go` holds
-- exactly one row IFF all eight preconditions passed, and EVERY write below
-- carries `(SELECT COUNT(*) FROM _mac642_go) = 1`. If any precondition failed,
-- `_mac642_go` is EMPTY and all 709 writes match zero rows. Fail-closed under
-- ANY runner, dot-command or not. This is the belt-and-braces MAC-661 adds to
-- mig-0049; 0051 carries the same shape.
-- MAC-642 GO GATE FAIL: one or more preconditions PRE-1..PRE-8 did not pass
CREATE TEMP TABLE _mac642_go (ok INTEGER CHECK (ok = 1));
INSERT INTO _mac642_go(ok) SELECT CASE WHEN (
       (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM _mac642_pre_1fail) = 1
   AND (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM _mac642_pre_2fail) = 1
   AND (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM _mac642_pre_3fail) = 1
   AND (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM _mac642_pre_4fail) = 1
   AND (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM _mac642_pre_5fail) = 1
   AND (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM _mac642_pre_6fail) = 1
   AND (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM _mac642_pre_7fail) = 1
   AND (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM _mac642_pre_8fail) = 1) THEN 1 ELSE 0 END;


-- ================================================================ ARM 1: RETYPE (654 rows)
-- ble_company_id -> ble_uuid, 16-bit value expanded to canonical 128-bit form.
